From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 17:34:58 +0000
Subject: fstep-stall: A pause or a window switch does not step the frame hold
 up

A frame shown for FSTEP_STALL (8) vsyncs or more is a stall (a pause, a covered
window, a fullscreen switch, a silent display link), not the scene's cost. It and
the FSTEP_GRACE frames after it do not count toward a step up. Before, the late
frames after every pause stepped the hold to 3: about a second at 20 and 30 fps
(Ocarina of Time, Mac M4 Pro). Headed upstream (seedds/nxnative).
---
 dm/gfx/nvn/hle_nvn.c         |  4 ++--
 dm/gfx/nvn/nvn_fstep.h       | 13 +++++++++++--
 dm/gfx/tests/t_fstep.c       | 24 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 docs/agents/symptoms.md      |  1 +
 docs/reference/frame-rate.md |  9 +++++++++
 5 files changed, 47 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

